# Nothing to ignore for llama-swap itself: it is a distro package living at
# /usr/bin/llama-swap, so no download, binary or upstream doc lands in this
# directory any more. The tarball-era rules went with the tarball, and README.md
# at the root is ours with no name to dodge.

# Loom's gufo, built by ./nix-loom-build.sh and pointed at the resulting
# /nix/store path by ./nix-loom-gufo.sh. Absolute symlinks into a store path that
# only exists on this box, so a clone gets two dead links and no hint. Build them
# yourself; loom/README.md walks through it.
/loom/gufo
/loom/gufo-server

# runtime droppings
*.log
*.pid
*.sock

# Agent-harness state. The tool working in this tree writes .pi/ next to its cwd,
# and a `git add -A` that only wanted the config takes it. Box-local session
# bookkeeping, not part of a routing config - and the next harness release can
# put anything at all in there.
.pi/
